  "summary": "Blücher, marching north to join Bernadotte before Leipzig, threw two pontoon bridges over the Elbe where the river bends round Wartenburg. Bertrand's corps held the far bank, Morand's French in the village behind a long dike, with marsh and backwaters in front. Yorck's corps crossed at dawn. Steinmetz's brigade attacked the dike head-on and was shot down; Mecklenburg's went upstream and drove the Württembergers out of Bleddin; and Horn's, wading through the mud, came in on the flank. Bertrand fell back on Kemberg, and the Army of Silesia was over the Elbe.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "label": "French Forces, Battle of Wartenberg, 3 October 1813 (Nafziger Collection 813JJB, after Mirus)",
