      "name": "Morand's Division",
      "formation": "12th Division, IV Corps (Bertrand)",
      "side": "French",
      "summary": "Bertrand's French division, posted in Wartenburg village and along the dike in front of it, which made a ready-made breastwork. It threw back Steinmetz's brigade, attacking straight across the open marshland, again and again, and only gave the village up when Horn's brigade came in on its flank.",
      "notes": [
        "Built from A Clash of Eagles' French 1812 list, the nearest to 1813: there is no list for the army Napoleon raised after Russia, largely of conscripts and of battalions drawn from depots all over the Empire.",
        "After Nafziger's order of battle for Wartenburg, from Mirus's history of the fight; its batteries are from his return of the IV Corps a fortnight before.",
        "Bertrand's corps was worn down by Dennewitz: a fortnight before, its battalions averaged about four hundred men, and some Italian regiments were down to a few hundred. They are shown at full size; the list's Small upgrade would suit many of them.",
        "The 13th and 23rd Line still had their regimental artillery companies, each shown as a section of regimental guns.",
        "The division's two foot batteries, where the list allows one, show as a historical departure.",
        "Commanders are at Staff Rating 8, the default for historical forces."
