      "side": "French",
      "summary": "All that was left of the Württemberg contingent, four combined battalions, holding Bleddin on Bertrand's right. Prince Karl of Mecklenburg's brigade came up the Elbe against it in the late morning, and by two in the afternoon had driven it out of the village.",
